/**
 * How one building's occupancy changes inside a what-if simulation — the per-building line item of
 * {@link CancelImpact#buildings} and the building-level detail behind {@link CloseImpact}.
 *
 * When a class is cancelled or a building is closed, the interesting consequence is rarely campus
 * wide; it is local and specific. This type carries that local answer: how many hours this
 * particular building newly loses its last class, whether that lets it power down earlier than the
 * saved plan already says, and which windows open up.
 *
 * Nothing here is committed. Simulations run against a scenario copy of the occupancy grid, so the
 * saved {@link MoveRecommendation} set and {@link BuildingHour} rows are untouched until the user
 * clicks "Apply to plan". Plain, non-persisted value type.
 */
type BuildingImpact {

  /**
   * Name of the affected {@link Building} (a {@link Building#id}).
   */
  building: !string

  /**
   * Building-hours that go from occupied to empty in this building because of the simulated change.
   * Zero means the building still has other classes in every hour it was already running.
   */
  hoursFreed: int

  /**
   * How many of the simulated sections were meeting in this building — the cause of
   * {@link #hoursFreed}.
   */
  sectionsRemoved: int

  /**
   * True when the change extends an existing setback window or creates a new one, i.e. the building
   * can genuinely go into setback earlier than the currently saved plan allows. False when hours
   * were freed but they sit inside a stretch that was already empty, so there is no new saving.
   */
  canPowerDownEarlier: boolean

  /**
   * The merged class-free windows this building gains under the simulation, each phrased as a
   * sentence. Windows with {@link SetbackWindow#newlyFreed} true are the ones the agent highlights
   * on the map.
   */
  windows: [SetbackWindow]

  /**
   * The impact as one plain-English sentence, e.g.
   * {@code "Siebel Center drops from 3 classes to 0 on Friday 2-3pm, so it can set back 1 hour earlier."}
   * Composed on the backend from the fields above so the agent's prose can never disagree with its
   * own numbers.
   */
  sentence: !string

  /**
   * Latitude of the building, from {@link Building#lat}, so the agent can fly the map to it.
   */
  lat: double

  /**
   * Longitude of the building, from {@link Building#lon}.
   */
  lon: double
}
